From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 14:45:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: bcm4377: restore private PCI windows
 before J713 resume

Shared radio PERST resets private BAR windows that generic PCI saved
state does not cover. Restore the windows and subsystem control in
resume_noirq, before interrupts or UNQUIESCE access the retained device.
Without this, Wi-Fi returns after sleep but Bluetooth HCI commands time
out. Restoring the windows permits Read Local Version to complete.

Coordinate QUIESCE and recovery work with the managed host transaction,
leaving other controllers on their existing path. Cover config failures
and retained-path skips with a fault-injection fixture.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
[niteria: bcm4377-resume-tests' mocks now have the radio sleep hooks]
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 6745e46a8030efcd28f9d3612344845866e6ebe7)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
